   "text": "**Cold drops tap the glass,**\n**Gold leaves drift in muddy streams,**\n**Earth exhales its breath.**\n\n### Imagery Explanation\n\nThis haiku relies on sensory details to evoke the specific mood of autumn rain:\n\n1.  **Auditory and Tactile (\"Cold drops tap the glass\")**: The first line establishes the immediate physical sensation of the rain. The word \"cold\" sets the temperature, while \"tap\" provides a gentle, rhythmic sound, suggesting a quiet, persistent rain rather than a violent storm. The \"glass\" implies the observer is indoors, watching the weather unfold, creating a sense of separation and contemplation.\n\n2.  **Visual (\"Gold leaves drift in muddy streams\")**: This line paints a vivid picture of the season\u2019s decay and beauty. \"Gold leaves\" contrasts with the grayness of the rain, highlighting the vibrant colors of autumn. The image of them \"drifting in muddy streams\" suggests movement and the inevitable cycle",
